Reuse rather than copy. Factor anything the controller editor and the keyboard editor share (the roster layer, the editor shell, row art, category headings, the confirm dialogs, conflict list rendering) into shared helpers where it is clean to do so. Don't make a second roster implementation.

- **Roster layer.** The shared fighter roster, titled "Customize keyboard controls", kicker "Settings", the same line saying the choice does not change the fighter played, all 48 slots, locked slots never open. The interaction is identical to the controller roster.
